@*
    The roadmap band: the planning view that sits above the panes rather than
    beside them, because a plan is read across time and the panes are read down a
    list.

    It is empty on purpose. The band exists so the layout has the row a timeline
    will be drawn in — the shell caps it at a quarter of the screen and the
    content div below owns the scrollbar, so RoadmapTimeline can be dropped
    straight in without the outer layout moving. What it will draw is selected
    Backlog Entries placed by their dates; a Roadmap owns neither status nor
    priority, it reads both from the entries it displays, which is why nothing
    here promises a plan of its own.

    The placeholder carries roadmap-band__empty because the library's empty state
    is shaped for a large empty pane and does not fit a quarter of a short window;
    the shell compacts it through that hook, drops its description below a 48rem
    viewport height, and hides the band altogether below 34rem.

    Whether the band is on screen is decided in the shell's header, in the same
    strip that shows and hides Inbox and Backlog. That is a binary: the band is
    either here at its normal size or it is not rendered at all. So there is no
    affordance on the band itself and no state of its own to hold — no parameters,
    nothing to fold, and the shell's grid has one track to drop rather than one to
    shrink.
*@

<section class="roadmap-band" id="roadmap-band" aria-labelledby="roadmap-band-title" data-testid="roadmap-band">
    <header class="roadmap-band__header">
        <p class="roadmap-band__eyebrow">Planning</p>
        <h2 id="roadmap-band-title" class="roadmap-band__title">Roadmap</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="roadmap-band__content" data-testid="roadmap-band-content">
        <EmptyState TestId="roadmap-band-empty-state"
                    CssClass="roadmap-band__empty"
                    Title="No roadmap yet"
                    Description="Planned backlog entries will appear here on a timeline. Status and priority are read from the entries themselves." />
    </div>
</section>
